{"module":"Term 2","title":"Unit 7 — The Arts","description":"Music, cinema, painting and heritage; the passive voice; expressing opinions.","intro":"This unit explores art forms and cultural heritage, including Moroccan arts.","objectifs":["Use arts vocabulary.","Form the passive (present and past).","Express and justify opinions."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>painting, sculpture, calligraphy, pottery, a masterpiece, an exhibition, a gallery</li><li>music: a band, a singer, lyrics ; cinema: a director, an actor, a plot, a film review</li><li>heritage: zellige, Gnawa music, traditional crafts</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: the passive voice","h":"<div class=\"formula key\">be (am / is / are / was / were) + past participle (+ by …)</div><ul><li>Active: <i>Picasso <b>painted</b> Guernica.</i> → Passive: <i>Guernica <b>was painted</b> by Picasso.</i></li><li>Present: <i>Zellige <b>is made</b> by hand.</i></li><li>We use the passive when the action is more important than the doer.</li></ul>"},{"t":"Communication: opinions","h":"<ul><li>In my opinion… / I think… / As far as I’m concerned…</li><li>Agreeing: I agree with you. — Disagreeing: I’m afraid I don’t agree.</li></ul>"}],"recap":"Passive = be + past participle; the tense is carried by “be” (is made / was made). Opinions: In my opinion…, I think…, I (don’t) agree.","cards":[["Passive","be + past participle"],["was painted","Past simple passive"],["a masterpiece","An artist’s best work"],["In my opinion","To give your opinion"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"This mosque ___ in the 12th century.","choices":["was built","built","is build","was build"],"answer":0,"explain":"Past passive: was + past participle (built)."},{"type":"direct","q":"The person who makes a film is the ___.","accept":["director"],"display":"director","explain":"The director directs the film."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Which expression gives an opinion?","choices":["In my opinion","For example","In conclusion","Moreover"],"answer":0,"explain":"“In my opinion” introduces your opinion."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Passive of “People speak Arabic in Morocco.”:","choices":["Arabic is spoken in Morocco.","Arabic was spoken in Morocco.","Arabic speaks in Morocco.","Arabic is speak in Morocco."],"answer":0,"explain":"Present simple → is + past participle (spoken)."},{"type":"direct","q":"Past participle of “write”:","accept":["written"],"display":"written","explain":"write – wrote – written."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“I’m afraid I don’t agree” is used to…","choices":["disagree politely","agree strongly","say you are scared","ask for information"],"answer":0,"explain":"Polite disagreement."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Passive of “The artist painted these pictures in 1990.”:","choices":["These pictures were painted by the artist in 1990.","These pictures was painted by the artist in 1990.","These pictures are painted by the artist in 1990.","The artist was painted these pictures in 1990."],"answer":0,"explain":"Plural subject + past → were + past participle."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete in the passive: “The exhibition ___ (open) by the minister yesterday.” (2 words)","accept":["was opened"],"display":"was opened","explain":"Past simple passive: was + opened."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Why do we use the passive in “The Koutoubia was built in the 12th century”?","choices":["The building is more important than who built it.","Because it is a question.","Because the subject is a person.","Because the verb is irregular."],"answer":0,"explain":"The focus is on the action / object, not the doer."}]}}